Two versions of a file use one function from lodash:

```js
// Version 1
const _ = require('lodash');
export const onType = _.debounce(search, 300);

// Version 2
import { debounce } from 'lodash-es';
export const onType = debounce(search, 300);
```

With a production build, Version 1 pulls the whole of lodash into the bundle and Version 2 includes little more than `debounce` and its helpers. Why?

