A like counter updates optimistically and should roll back when the request fails. The post starts at 10 likes, the user clicks once, and the request fails. What count is shown afterwards, and what is the right fix?

```jsx
function LikeCount({ postId, initialCount }) {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);

  async function like() {
    setCount(count + 1);          // optimistic
    try {
      await api.like(postId);
    } catch {
      setCount(count - 1);        // roll back
    }
  }

  return <button onClick={like}>♥ {count}</button>;
}
```

